From d9df31eae7c60a2bc133c60f04ba4ba6e7322fb7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EchoChat Assistant <assistant@echochat.local>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 16:05:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix responsive layout bugs, localize hardcoded strings, and
 add optional Firebase cloud sync

Responsive / UI fixes:
- Channel list rail used a fixed 320dp width on wide screens; now scales
  with available width (280-380dp) so it looks right on tablets too.
- Message input bar had no IME padding, so the keyboard could cover it;
  added imePadding() and windowSoftInputMode=adjustResize.
- ModalBottomSheet (profile/settings) stretched full-width on desktop-size
  windows; now capped at 480dp and centered.
- Post cards in Explore/Saved/Profile stretched full-width on wide screens;
  now capped at 640dp and centered, matching the channel list treatment.
- Fixed a fragile dark-mode detection in MessageBubble that compared a
  Color's raw bit value against a hardcoded constant; now uses luminance().
- Removed a pre-existing duplicate  in DialogsAndSheets.kt.

Localization:
- Seven hardcoded Persian/English mixed strings (post category label,
  channel icon label, contact name label, suggested contacts label,
  avatar color label, shared posts title, and several content
  descriptions) now go through EchoStrings instead of bypassing i18n.
- Added a test asserting the newly localized keys exist in both languages.

Optional Firebase backend (additive, inert unless configured):
- FirebaseAuthManager: Google Sign-In via Credential Manager, using a
  SHA-256-hashed nonce (API 24-safe, avoids java.util.Base64).
- FirestoreSyncManager: one-way-per-direction bridge between Room and
  Firestore for channels and messages, with exactly one listener/collector
  per channel to avoid leaks. Local Room data remains the source of truth
  the UI reads from; nothing in the ViewModel/Repository/Compose layer had
  to change for screens to keep working with or without sync enabled.
- EchoChatViewModel now exposes accountState/signInWithGoogle/signOut,
  gated behind FirebaseApp.getApps(context).isNotEmpty() so the sign-in UI
  is hidden entirely when no real Firebase project is linked.
- ChannelEntity/MessageEntity given default values for every field so
  Firestore's toObject() (which needs a no-arg constructor) can deserialize
  them; verified every existing call site already used named arguments.
- Uncommented the already-scaffolded firebase-firestore/firebase-auth/
  credentials/googleid dependencies; added the missing
  kotlinx-coroutines-play-services dependency required for Task.await().
- Added app/FIREBASE_SETUP.md with full setup steps (Firebase project,
  google-services.json, Web client ID, Firestore security rules) and
  documented current sync limitations (channels/messages only, full-resend
  push strategy, IGNORE conflict policy).
- Updated README.md to describe the new optional sync path accurately.
